 34MG  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34MG  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34MG2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34MG c  Fragmentation of {+40}Ar beams with {+9}Be target to obtain secondary  
 34MG2c  beam of {+36}Si                                                        
 34MG c  2001Yo03 (also 2002Sa11,2002Yo04,2002Mo35): a 95-MeV/nucleon, 60-pnA   
 34MG2c  primary beam of {+40}Ar bombarded a 462.5-mg/cm2 {+9}Be primary target.
 34MG3c  A secondary beam of {+36}Si was separated by the the RIKEN             
 34MG4c  projectile-fragment separator RIPS and transported to a secondary      
 34MG5c  target of 385.5-mg/cm2 {+9}Be at a center-of-target energy of 38       
 34MG6c  MeV/nucleon. Reaction products from the 36Si+9Be fragmentation were    
 34MG7c  detected and identified at forward angles with a parallel plate        
 34MG8c  avalanche counter (PPAC) and four sets of counter telescopes, each     
 34MG9c  consisting of three silicon detectors and one Si(Li) detector. |g rays 
 34MGAc  emitted from excited fragments were detected using 55 NaI(Tl)          
 34MGBc  detectors. Measured E|g with Doppler correction, I|g, ({+34}Mg)|g-coin,
 34MGCc  and |g|g-coin. Deduced levels. Compared with shell-model calculations  
 34MGDc  using the SPDF-M effective interaction. {+9}Be({+36}Si,X|g) E=38       
 34MGEc  MeV/nucleon. {+36}Si beam obtained from {+9}Be({+40}Ar,X) at 95        
 34MGFc  MeV/nucleon. RIKEN-RIPS facility, time-of-flight and energy loss       
 34MGGc  measurements to identify fragments. Measured E|g, (fragment)|g coin,   
 34MGHc  yields, array of 66 NaI(Tl) detectors.                                 
